  railChallengeTutorials:
  - id: 811
    title: "Locked Side"
    body: "The {side} rail is closed. Red stripes and a lock mark the blocked side. Drag the magnet around the other three sides to guide the ball."
    buttonLabel: GOT IT
    completionTooltip: "Plan your route using the open rails"
  - id: 812
    title: "Limited Rail"
    body: "Only the unstriped section of the {side} rail is available. The other three sides remain open. Use a different angle when a blocked section stops your drag."
    buttonLabel: GOT IT
    completionTooltip: "Use the unstriped rail section"
  - id: 813
    title: "Timed Lock"
    body: "The {side} rail opens and closes. Green means open; red stripes mean locked. Watch the countdown. If it closes while your magnet is there, the field pauses until it opens, or you move to another side."
    buttonLabel: GOT IT
    completionTooltip: "Watch the rail countdown and time your pulls"
  - id: 814
    title: "Unlock Switch"
    body: "Guide the ball over the colored switch inside the board. It turns green and permanently unlocks the {side} rail and goal for this attempt."
    buttonLabel: GOT IT
    completionTooltip: "Hit the switch before heading for the goal"
  - id: 815
    title: "Side Change Limit"
    body: "This level gives you {budget} changes between magnet sides. Moving along the same side costs nothing. Plan your route before switching; Restart gives you a fresh budget."
    buttonLabel: GOT IT
    completionTooltip: "The remaining side changes are shown below the board"
  - id: 816
    title: "Magnet Cooldown"
    body: "Long pulls drain the magnet charge. When empty, the magnet briefly recharges and the ball coasts. Release early to cool it down, and use short pulls to stay in control."
    buttonLabel: GOT IT
    completionTooltip: "Watch the charge bar and let the ball coast while recharging"
  firstTimeTutorials:
  - id: 101
    title: Move the magnet
    body: Touch and drag the magnet around the outside edge of the glass. The magnet
      stays outside; the ball stays inside.
    buttonLabel: NEXT
    completionTooltip: 
  - id: 102
    title: Guide the ball
    body: Hold the magnet to attract the steel ball. Release to let it coast, then
      guide it into the glowing green pocket.
    buttonLabel: NEXT
    completionTooltip: 
  - id: 103
    title: Use energy wisely
    body: Your magnetic field uses energy while you hold and move the magnet. Finish
      with less energy to earn more stars.
    buttonLabel: LET'S PLAY
    completionTooltip: Drag the magnet to begin
  secondLevelTutorials:
  - id: 111
    title: Walls block force
    body: A wall removes only the ball's motion into it. Slide along the wall, then
      move the magnet to another side to route around the corner.
    buttonLabel: SHOW ME
    completionTooltip: Use another side of the glass when the direct pull is blocked
  - id: 112
    title: Release and redirect
    body: You do not need to hold the magnet forever. Release to let the ball coast,
      then grab the magnet again from a better side.
    buttonLabel: LET'S TRY
    completionTooltip: Short controlled pulls are easier than one long pull
  echoMagnetTutorial:
    id: 801
    title: Echo Magnet
    body: Tap ECHO, then drag the magnet. Your recorded path repeats as a cyan ghost
      while you control the real magnet. Both fields combine.
    buttonLabel: RECORD AN ECHO
    completionTooltip: Record a path, then steer beside your ghost
  ferrofluidTutorial:
    id: 802
    title: Ferrofluid Memory
    body: The ball leaves a conductive trail. When it crosses its trail again, the
      remembered direction helps guide its momentum.
    buttonLabel: FOLLOW THE TRAIL
    completionTooltip: 
  magneticImprintTutorial:
    id: 803
    title: Magnetic Imprints
    body: Striped metal walls wake when the ball touches them. Blue imprints pull
      and red imprints push for a few seconds.
    buttonLabel: WAKE THE WALLS
    completionTooltip: 
  fieldLensTutorial:
    id: 804
    title: Field Lenses
    body: Purple lenses rotate magnetic force. Watch the arrow inside each lens before
      committing to a pull.
    buttonLabel: BEND THE FIELD
    completionTooltip: 
  polarityLockTutorial:
    id: 805
    title: Polarity Locks
    body: Follow the PULL and PUSH symbols on the lock using the force button. Completed symbols turn green. Finish the sequence to open the passage.
    buttonLabel: ENTER THE CODE
    completionTooltip: 
  orbitGoalTutorial:
    id: 806
    title: Orbit Goal
    body: The pocket opens only after the ball circles its green ring. Build sideways
      momentum, complete the orbit, then drop into the centre.
    buttonLabel: ENTER ORBIT
    completionTooltip: 
  chapters:
  - title: Magnetic Basics
    challenge: Learn smooth, efficient pulls
